      "contentSha256": "eca7114a5c78267ec61604bbe4ee707a0aa3a3b5f13dad610390de427fc5b0af",
      "supersedes": "Ambiguous use of already completed in the 2026-08-01 ECO 461 concurrency wording",
      "statement": "For the existing ECO 461 concurrency exception, exactly one of ECO 213 or ECO 214 must be successfully completed before the target ECO 461 term. Eligible completed and accepted-transfer evidence, a current in-progress course finishing before the target term, and an earlier generated-term course may count. Same-term or later courses and uncertain or unaccepted history, equivalency, substitution, waiver, or prerequisite evidence do not count. Earlier in-progress or planned completion remains conditional on success. This clarifies the existing 2026-08-01 department-confirmed exception and creates no new exception or alternate planning mode."
    },
